WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.845
The On-Chain Operator calculator.

00:00:02.845 --> 00:00:04.795
Twenty tools, one habit.

00:00:04.795 --> 00:00:06.330
You bring a live rate.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.075
The picture tells you whether the idea still holds.

00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:11.755
Here's the problem.

00:00:11.755 --> 00:00:14.070
A headline rate is not a decision.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.644
A pool can quote a high fee

00:00:15.644 --> 00:00:17.800
while a price move beats holding.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.664
A loan can look cheap until price

00:00:19.664 --> 00:00:21.145
hits a line you never drew.

00:00:22.445 --> 00:00:25.040
A common shortcut is to trust the card.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.955
The card already did the math.

00:00:26.955 --> 00:00:29.102
That belief fails the moment the card

00:00:29.102 --> 00:00:32.000
used yesterday's rate, or someone else's hope.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.980
You still supply the live rate.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.135
This file only checks the rate you type.

00:00:37.435 --> 00:00:38.587
By the end, you'll be

00:00:38.587 --> 00:00:40.143
able to do three things.

00:00:40.143 --> 00:00:42.848
Pick the one tool that matches the question.

00:00:42.848 --> 00:00:45.878
Type live rates, in the form the field expects.

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:48.283
And read the band, before you size anything.

00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:52.163
Every tool runs the same four beats.

00:00:52.163 --> 00:00:53.688
Start with your inputs.

00:00:53.688 --> 00:00:54.954
Those are the rates you

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.573
type, from a live source.

00:00:56.573 --> 00:00:58.608
The picture updates as you type.

00:00:58.608 --> 00:00:59.808
Then the band.

00:00:59.808 --> 00:01:02.268
Green means inside the lesson's buffer.

00:01:02.268 --> 00:01:03.853
Blue means watch this.

00:01:03.853 --> 00:01:05.848
Red means outside that buffer.

00:01:05.848 --> 00:01:07.333
Last, your decision.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.628
Act, or wait.

00:01:08.628 --> 00:01:10.893
The band is a model of the inputs.

00:01:10.893 --> 00:01:12.131
It is not a promise,

00:01:12.131 --> 00:01:13.368
and it is not advice.

00:01:14.668 --> 00:01:16.260
Read the band and the figure

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:17.933
before you touch a field.

00:01:17.933 --> 00:01:20.473
Change the lesson example, which is already

00:01:20.473 --> 00:01:22.678
filled in, by editing one number.

00:01:22.678 --> 00:01:24.434
Watch the band change colour when

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.283
that number leaves the buffer.

00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:27.929
Search any of the twenty tools

00:01:27.929 --> 00:01:29.363
once you know the question.

00:01:30.663 --> 00:01:33.528
A liquidation threshold is eighty percent.

00:01:33.528 --> 00:01:34.993
What do you type in that field?

00:01:39.413 --> 00:01:41.468
The answer is point eight zero.

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:43.598
The field runs from zero to one, so

00:01:43.598 --> 00:01:46.083
eighty percent is point eight, not eighty.

00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:50.007
Open impermanent loss when the question is

00:01:50.007 --> 00:01:52.448
the gap versus simply holding, and type

00:01:52.448 --> 00:01:54.518
the move you actually expect.

00:01:54.518 --> 00:01:56.764
Open fee break-even when you know that

00:01:56.764 --> 00:01:58.491
gap, and type the fee you can

00:01:58.491 --> 00:02:00.403
see, not a fee you hope for.

00:02:00.403 --> 00:02:03.092
Open concentrated range and type the lower

00:02:03.092 --> 00:02:05.768
and upper prices you would really set.

00:02:05.768 --> 00:02:09.254
Open loss versus rebalancing for a full-range pool, and

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:11.868
type volatility and the fee you see today.

00:02:13.168 --> 00:02:16.279
Here is the lesson example for impermanent loss.

00:02:16.279 --> 00:02:18.594
The price multiple is two, a double.

00:02:18.594 --> 00:02:21.179
The baseline is to hold both assets.

00:02:21.179 --> 00:02:23.424
The pool keeps a fifty-fifty mix, so

00:02:23.424 --> 00:02:25.847
it sells the winner as price rises.

00:02:25.847 --> 00:02:28.302
A half, point five, mirrors this gap.

00:02:28.302 --> 00:02:30.437
The result is a gap versus holding

00:02:30.437 --> 00:02:33.056
of about five point seven two percent.

00:02:33.056 --> 00:02:35.081
Use this before you trust a fee quote.

00:02:36.381 --> 00:02:38.436
Why fee break-even exists.

00:02:38.436 --> 00:02:40.177
Hope says type a fee you wish

00:02:40.177 --> 00:02:42.208
for, ignore how long you stay, and

00:02:42.208 --> 00:02:43.611
call any fee a win.

00:02:43.611 --> 00:02:45.682
The check says type the fee you can

00:02:45.682 --> 00:02:47.810
see, type the move and the days, and

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.606
ask if fees cover the gap.

00:02:49.606 --> 00:02:51.159
In the lesson, a one and a

00:02:51.159 --> 00:02:53.403
half times move over thirty days still

00:02:53.403 --> 00:02:55.946
trails holding at a twenty percent fee.

00:02:55.946 --> 00:02:58.586
It needs about twenty-five percent to break even.

00:02:59.886 --> 00:03:02.111
Best use, for the four pool tools.

00:03:02.111 --> 00:03:04.510
Impermanent loss: type two for a double,

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.331
and point five for a half.

00:03:06.331 --> 00:03:08.412
Fee break-even: the fee on the pool

00:03:08.412 --> 00:03:10.736
today, plus how long you will stay.

00:03:10.736 --> 00:03:14.513
Concentrated range: your real lower and upper prices.

00:03:14.513 --> 00:03:17.916
A range from eighteen hundred to thirty-two hundred works

00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:20.732
the lesson capital about seven and a half times

00:03:20.732 --> 00:03:23.731
harder, and that work stops when price leaves.

00:03:23.731 --> 00:03:25.639
Loss versus rebalancing is the

00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:28.401
full-range case, before you concentrate.

00:03:28.401 --> 00:03:31.721
Eighty percent volatility is an eight percent drag.

00:03:31.721 --> 00:03:33.396
Fees have to clear that drag.

00:03:34.696 --> 00:03:37.181
Open health factor before you borrow.

00:03:37.181 --> 00:03:39.175
It shows how far the loan sits from

00:03:39.175 --> 00:03:41.801
liquidation, and the price that closes it.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.884
Open the lending loop to see what

00:03:43.884 --> 00:03:47.186
repeated borrow-and-supply does to your exposure.

00:03:47.186 --> 00:03:49.630
Open the supply rate to turn the borrow

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:52.985
rate, utilisation, and reserve into the lend rate.

00:03:52.985 --> 00:03:54.868
Open the mint tool for how many

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:57.340
stablecoins a vault allows, and the price

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.405
that breaks its minimum ratio.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:02.974
Open perp liquidation for the approximate price that

00:04:02.974 --> 00:04:06.610
closes an isolated perpetual, before fees and funding.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:09.475
Work the lesson loan.

00:04:09.475 --> 00:04:12.555
Collateral is ten units at three thousand dollars.

00:04:12.555 --> 00:04:15.660
The liquidation threshold is point eight zero.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.690
Debt is ten thousand dollars.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.290
Health factor equals collateral, times the

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:22.465
threshold, divided by the debt.

00:04:22.465 --> 00:04:24.392
The result is a health factor of

00:04:24.392 --> 00:04:26.844
two point four zero, and liquidation near

00:04:26.844 --> 00:04:29.655
one thousand two hundred and fifty dollars.

00:04:29.655 --> 00:04:31.920
That is the price where the buffer is gone.

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:34.875
Why this tool exists.

00:04:34.875 --> 00:04:36.800
A protocol will not call you.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.854
Double the debt, to twenty thousand dollars, and the

00:04:39.854 --> 00:04:42.575
health factor falls to one point two zero.

00:04:42.575 --> 00:04:44.179
That is under the one point

00:04:44.179 --> 00:04:46.140
five floor this program uses.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.135
Repay, or add collateral.

00:04:48.135 --> 00:04:50.187
At ten thousand dollars of debt, the

00:04:50.187 --> 00:04:52.540
health factor is two point four zero.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.716
There is room above two point zero,

00:04:54.716 --> 00:04:57.010
and liquidation is far from spot.

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:59.161
Best use: type today's price, and

00:04:59.161 --> 00:05:01.565
the protocol's threshold as a decimal.

00:05:02.865 --> 00:05:05.520
Best use, for the other four borrowing tools.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.248
Lending loop: type the loan-to-value you will

00:05:08.248 --> 00:05:10.561
really use, the passes you will really

00:05:10.561 --> 00:05:12.284
do, and both live rates.

00:05:12.284 --> 00:05:15.029
In the lesson, three passes at point seven

00:05:15.029 --> 00:05:18.286
five, with five percent supplied and three percent

00:05:18.286 --> 00:05:21.395
borrowed, lever about two point seven times.

00:05:21.395 --> 00:05:23.396
The spread in that example vanishes

00:05:23.396 --> 00:05:25.585
near an eight percent borrow rate.

00:05:25.585 --> 00:05:28.747
Supply rate: borrow rate, times utilisation,

00:05:28.747 --> 00:05:31.015
times one minus the reserve.

00:05:31.015 --> 00:05:33.480
Eight percent, times point seven, times

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.875
point nine, is about five percent.

00:05:35.875 --> 00:05:38.784
Mint: type one hundred and fifty to mean one

00:05:38.784 --> 00:05:42.380
hundred and fifty percent, not one point five zero.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.275
The lesson vault can mint up to

00:05:44.275 --> 00:05:46.288
twenty thousand, and a fee of two

00:05:46.288 --> 00:05:48.716
percent is one hundred and sixty dollars

00:05:48.716 --> 00:05:50.970
a year on an eight thousand mint.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:53.520
Perp: a long closes below the entry.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.295
A short closes above it.

00:05:55.295 --> 00:05:57.484
A five times long from three thousand,

00:05:57.484 --> 00:06:00.345
with a half percent maintenance margin, liquidates

00:06:00.345 --> 00:06:02.085
near two thousand four hundred.

00:06:03.385 --> 00:06:05.790
Ten units at three thousand dollars.

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:07.625
Threshold point eight zero.

00:06:07.625 --> 00:06:09.410
Debt ten thousand dollars.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:10.735
What is the health factor?

00:06:15.155 --> 00:06:17.430
The answer is two point four zero.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.510
Collateral times the threshold, divided by the debt.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.375
Open funding carry for what one eight-hour

00:06:24.375 --> 00:06:26.522
funding print means on a hedge, and

00:06:26.522 --> 00:06:28.910
for what the short leg can survive.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.917
Open cash and carry for the gap

00:06:30.917 --> 00:06:33.174
between a dated future and spot, if

00:06:33.174 --> 00:06:35.230
you can hold both to expiry.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.452
Open the covered call for the premium

00:06:37.452 --> 00:06:39.850
you keep this period, not the annualised

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:42.665
figure, because a short window inflates it.

00:06:42.665 --> 00:06:44.986
Open the principal token for the fixed

00:06:44.986 --> 00:06:47.307
result of buying below one and holding

00:06:47.307 --> 00:06:49.035
to maturity, if it pays.

00:06:49.035 --> 00:06:52.435
Open rate to compounded rate to see what compounding

00:06:52.435 --> 00:06:55.643
adds, and whether gas eats the extra transactions.

00:06:56.943 --> 00:06:58.513
Best use for funding.

00:06:58.513 --> 00:07:00.801
Point zero one percent means point

00:07:00.801 --> 00:07:03.323
zero one percent, not one percent.

00:07:03.323 --> 00:07:05.553
In the lesson, that print each eight

00:07:05.553 --> 00:07:07.903
hours, at two times leverage, is about

00:07:07.903 --> 00:07:10.254
eleven percent a year on the position,

00:07:10.254 --> 00:07:12.603
and less on the capital behind it.

00:07:12.603 --> 00:07:13.998
Funding can flip.

00:07:13.998 --> 00:07:15.915
Then you are the one paying it, and

00:07:15.915 --> 00:07:18.346
the short still has a liquidation price.

00:07:18.346 --> 00:07:21.086
Type the live print, not last month's average.

00:07:22.387 --> 00:07:24.592
Best use, for the other yield tools.

00:07:24.592 --> 00:07:26.493
Cash and carry: type spot, the

00:07:26.493 --> 00:07:28.387
future, and the days left.

00:07:28.387 --> 00:07:30.226
A two dollar gap on a hundred

00:07:30.226 --> 00:07:32.617
dollar spot, with thirty days left, is

00:07:32.617 --> 00:07:35.436
two percent raw and about twenty-four percent

00:07:35.436 --> 00:07:38.127
annualised, only if you hold to expiry.

00:07:38.127 --> 00:07:40.312
Covered call: a one-week premium is

00:07:40.312 --> 00:07:41.887
not a year of income.

00:07:41.887 --> 00:07:44.295
Spot one hundred, strike one hundred and

00:07:44.295 --> 00:07:46.769
ten, premium two percent, seven days.

00:07:46.769 --> 00:07:49.180
The most you keep in that example is twelve

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:52.329
percent, and the premium is used up at ninety-eight.

00:07:52.329 --> 00:07:55.783
Principal token: point nine five means you pay point

00:07:55.783 --> 00:07:58.495
nine five to receive one, if it pays.

00:07:58.495 --> 00:07:59.935
Ninety days in the lesson

00:07:59.935 --> 00:08:02.230
is about twenty-three percent fixed.

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:05.155
The risk is whether it pays, not the formula.

00:08:05.155 --> 00:08:08.851
Compounding: twelve percent, compounded twelve times, is

00:08:08.851 --> 00:08:12.004
about twelve point seven percent before gas.

00:08:12.004 --> 00:08:15.384
Check gas against the position before you compound again.

00:08:16.684 --> 00:08:19.393
Open risk-adjusted yield to take a headline

00:08:19.393 --> 00:08:21.239
rate down by a loss you might

00:08:21.239 --> 00:08:23.571
actually take, and by your costs.

00:08:23.571 --> 00:08:26.141
Open the income plan to do that across every

00:08:26.141 --> 00:08:29.411
position, then choose a payout that leaves a buffer.

00:08:29.411 --> 00:08:32.492
Open the balance sheet for equity, your loan-to-value

00:08:32.492 --> 00:08:35.246
rule, health factor, and months of reserve.

00:08:35.246 --> 00:08:38.560
Open time-weighted return when deposits are mixed into

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.451
the gain, and you want the decisions alone.

00:08:41.451 --> 00:08:44.688
Open airdrop value with an honest chance, the amount

00:08:44.688 --> 00:08:47.676
if it arrives, and every cost of chasing it.

00:08:47.676 --> 00:08:49.280
Open value at risk for a

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:51.826
one-day loss floor from volatility.

00:08:51.826 --> 00:08:54.333
Crypto crashes run past a normal model,

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.276
so treat the number as a floor.

00:08:57.576 --> 00:08:59.901
Risk-adjusted yield, in the lesson.

00:08:59.901 --> 00:09:01.866
The headline is twelve percent.

00:09:01.866 --> 00:09:04.223
The chance of a hit is point zero five,

00:09:04.223 --> 00:09:07.411
and that hit takes forty percent of the position.

00:09:07.411 --> 00:09:09.046
Costs are one percent.

00:09:09.046 --> 00:09:13.026
Twelve, minus point zero five times forty, minus one.

00:09:13.026 --> 00:09:14.920
The result is about nine percent

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.056
after that loss and those costs.

00:09:17.056 --> 00:09:18.661
Best use: the chance and the

00:09:18.661 --> 00:09:20.621
share lost are your estimates.

00:09:20.621 --> 00:09:22.666
A wishful chance prints a wishful nine.

00:09:23.966 --> 00:09:26.041
Three ways the book gets misread.

00:09:26.041 --> 00:09:28.836
People spend the whole modelled income, mix

00:09:28.836 --> 00:09:31.632
deposits into the return, and treat one-day

00:09:31.632 --> 00:09:33.901
value at risk as the worst day.

00:09:33.901 --> 00:09:35.041
Best use.

00:09:35.041 --> 00:09:37.461
Keep a buffer, as in the income plan.

00:09:37.461 --> 00:09:39.935
The lesson book of one hundred and fifty

00:09:39.935 --> 00:09:43.556
thousand models about thirteen thousand of expected income,

00:09:43.556 --> 00:09:46.452
pays out about seventy percent, and keeps about

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:48.321
four thousand as a buffer.

00:09:48.321 --> 00:09:50.611
Split the record at every deposit.

00:09:50.611 --> 00:09:53.169
The lesson stretches of five, minus two,

00:09:53.169 --> 00:09:55.352
and four percent are about a seven

00:09:55.352 --> 00:09:58.471
percent time-weighted return, close to the simple

00:09:58.471 --> 00:10:01.266
gain only because the deposit was small.

00:10:01.266 --> 00:10:03.726
Call value at risk a floor, not a cap.

00:10:03.726 --> 00:10:06.731
Fifty thousand dollars at eighty percent volatility

00:10:06.731 --> 00:10:08.349
is about a three and a half

00:10:08.349 --> 00:10:10.961
thousand dollar day in the normal model.

00:10:10.961 --> 00:10:12.361
Crash days can be worse.

00:10:13.661 --> 00:10:15.407
You might add liquidity, and you

00:10:15.407 --> 00:10:17.136
expect the price to double.

00:10:17.136 --> 00:10:19.011
Which pool tool do you open first?

00:10:23.431 --> 00:10:25.593
The answer is impermanent loss.

00:10:25.593 --> 00:10:27.146
Measure the gap versus holding

00:10:27.146 --> 00:10:28.398
before you trust the fee.

00:10:29.698 --> 00:10:30.768
Your turn.

00:10:30.768 --> 00:10:33.723
Open the calculator file on your own computer.

00:10:33.723 --> 00:10:35.359
Pick the tool that matches a

00:10:35.359 --> 00:10:37.633
position you already have on paper.

00:10:37.633 --> 00:10:40.513
Type the live numbers, not a hoped-for rate.

00:10:40.513 --> 00:10:41.955
Write down the band, and the

00:10:41.955 --> 00:10:43.648
one number you would act on.

00:10:43.648 --> 00:10:45.673
That takes five to twenty minutes.

00:10:45.673 --> 00:10:47.288
You do not need a wallet.

00:10:47.288 --> 00:10:49.532
Never type a seed phrase, a private

00:10:49.532 --> 00:10:51.713
key, or a password into this file,

00:10:51.713 --> 00:10:53.396
or into anything that asks.

00:10:54.696 --> 00:10:56.201
Three lines to keep.

00:10:56.201 --> 00:10:58.151
Twenty tools, one habit.

00:10:58.151 --> 00:11:00.546
Change one input, and read the band.

00:11:00.546 --> 00:11:02.523
The menu is pools, then borrowing,

00:11:02.523 --> 00:11:04.291
then yield, then the book.

00:11:04.291 --> 00:11:05.846
You supply the rates.

00:11:05.846 --> 00:11:07.528
The picture is a model, not

00:11:07.528 --> 00:11:09.149
a forecast, and not advice.

00:11:10.449 --> 00:11:12.337
Open the calculator and run one

00:11:12.337 --> 00:11:14.289
position before you size it.

00:11:14.289 --> 00:11:17.406
Next, take a health-factor loan back to lesson three

00:11:17.406 --> 00:11:19.994
point two, and say why a health factor near

00:11:19.994 --> 00:11:22.229
one is a closing price, not a cushion.
